  "semanticEquivalence": {
    "verdict": "exact_for_the_changed_schedule_under_the_frozen_batch_16_configuration",
    "controlTransformation": "tag = hint(raw, H) ? cycleTag(point, raw) : raw; H_control = histPush(H, tag)",
    "candidateTransformation": "hinted = hint(raw, H); H_raw = histPush(H, raw); if hinted, replace low16(H_raw) with cycleTag(point, raw); otherwise retain H_raw",
    "identity": "histPush(H,t) = ((H << 16) mod 2^64) | (t & 0xffff). Therefore (histPush(H,raw) & ~0xffff) | tag equals histPush(H,tag) whenever tag fits 16 bits.",
    "sourceFacts": [
      "The hint predicate is evaluated against the same pre-push history H in both schedules.",
      "twCycleTag receives the same point, raw tag, tables, and dpWeight and does not receive incoming walk history.",
      "Raw and resolved tags encode h, k, and eps and are at most 0x1827, so the low-16 replacement is lossless.",
      "No point or per-slot history advances between raw selection and hinted resolution.",
      "Each slot has a distinct history index. Resolving pending slots in different lane-local orders has no cross-slot data dependency.",
      "The addend pass reads the final low-16 tag only after all pending hints are resolved.",
      "The compile-time guard limits the mask to at most 64 slots; the measured batch has 16 slots."
    ],
